also references of EP     1103814A1</text><sources><source name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></nplcit></non-patent-citations></citations></technical-data><parties><applicants><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>MITSUBISHI CHEM CORP</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>TAKADA MAKOTO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>MITSUBISHI CHEMICAL CORPORATION</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TAKADA, MAKOTO</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>TAKADA MAKOTO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TAKADA, MAKOTO</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A pretreatment method for assaying a subject matter while eliminating effects of binding proteins coexisting in a biological sample, which comprises mixing the biological sample with at least one pretreatment agent selected from among surfactants and alkali agents; separating the binding proteins in the sample from the subject matter to be assayed; and, at the same time, inactivating the proteins by inducing irreversible denaturation.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'invention concerne un procédé de prétraitement permettant d'analyser une substance tout en éliminant les effets de protéines de liaison coexistant dans un échantillon biologique. Ce procédé consiste à mélanger l'échantillon biologique avec au moins un agent de prétraitement choisi parmi des tensioactifs et des agents alcalins, à séparer les protéines de liaison, contenues dans l'échantillon, de la substance à analyser, et, simultanément, à inactiver les protéines par induction d'une dénaturation irréversible.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>